@normanmaurer
```

int oneLength = 16,twoLength = 256;
// int elemSize = 4096; // normal
int elemSize = 8192; // unnormal
ByteBuf[] ones = new ByteBuf[oneLength];
ByteBuf[] twos = new ByteBuf[twoLength];
//allocate
for (int i = 0; i < oneLength; i++) {
    ones[i] = ByteBufAllocator.DEFAULT.buffer(elemSize, Integer.MAX_VALUE);
}
for (int i = 0; i < twoLength; i++) {
    twos[i] = ByteBufAllocator.DEFAULT.buffer(elemSize, Integer.MAX_VALUE);
}

//deallocate the 'tows', in oder to filled of PoolThreadCache.MemoryRegionCache.queue
for (int i = 0; i < twoLength; i++) {
    new WrappedCompositeByteBuf(compositeBuffer().addComponent(twos[i])).deallocate();
}
// when deallocate ones, the MemoryRegionCache.queue had been filled, 
for (int i = 0; i < oneLength; i++) {
    new WrappedCompositeByteBuf(compositeBuffer().addComponent(ones[i])).deallocate();
}

```
elemSize = 8192:
when all of ByteBuf be freed, the size of PoolChunk#subpages will be 256 + 16, and PoolSubpage two-way linked list size = 16

elemSIze = 4196;
the size of PoolChunk#subpages will be 256 + 1, PoolSubpage two-way linked list size = 1
